    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5867c728_bc5b8a2d",
        "filename": "common/usb_pd_protocol.c",
        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 2828,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-01-03T18:07:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What about SOP\u0027?  The spec indicates SOP\u0027 should be sent first followed by SOP\" and SOP last(section 5.4.3.3 of Type-C spec)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2828,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 2828,
        "endChar": 64
      },
      "revId": "59e151d76df7124bd95bf985fba435527c9dd48f",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "08e50608_11fdb6b5",
        "filename": "common/usb_pd_protocol.c",
        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 2837,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-01-03T18:07:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Reading the PD spec, I believe we shouldn\u0027t set these until after receiving an Accept.  Given the architecture of our non-VDM state machine, this may need its own state in this file so we can act after receiving our Accept.  \n\nBased on the sequence diagrams in the PD spec (section 8.3.2.15) and the above Type-C spec reference, I would guess we should do: Enter_USB SOP\u0027 -\u003e Accept SOP\u0027 -\u003e Enter_USB SOP -\u003e Accept SOP -\u003e start USB4 operation.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2836,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 2837,
        "endChar": 25
      },
      "revId": "59e151d76df7124bd95bf985fba435527c9dd48f",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
